From 9bb8a26f528370f3996d71bda9900f0688777a3b Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: WeiguangTWK <weiguangtwk@outlook.com>
Date: Wed, 11 Nov 2026 16:49:33 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] Neko LineageOS: [ASTER] restrict ASTER source credential keys
 to verified executors

Add authorization for dedicated ASTER source-credential namespaces.
Use the registered executor identity instead of relying only on the
caller's UID or SELinux domain.

Separate built-in and standalone collector credentials so the weaker
standalone execution boundary cannot authorize built-in credentials.

Validate stored descriptors when keys are accessed through KEY_ID or
GRANT, and bind credential operations to the authorized executor
generation. Reject protected-key import, transfer and namespace
migration paths.

Reuse existing hardware-backed key generation and HMAC operations.
Leave unrelated key namespaces and vendor KeyMint interfaces unchanged.

Change-Id: I55cf2bb2daa9432274dc7f6a8af4087dc95ebf39
